course: dictionary
lesson: 12275
title: Contradictory: when two things cannot both be true
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Two statements are contradictory when they say opposite things, so both cannot be true. «The bridge is open.» «The bridge is closed.» These two messages contradict each other, so one of them must be wrong.
explain: A contradictory person often says one thing and then the opposite. «First Sam said he loved peas, then he said he hated them.» Sam's words are contradictory, so we cannot be sure what he really thinks.
explain: Detectives listen hard for contradictory evidence. If one witness says the thief wore a red hat and another says it was blue, the stories cannot both be right. Ask yourself: can both be true? If not, the words are contradictory.
fact: Contradictory means saying opposite things, so both cannot be true.
fact: Contradictory is an adjective: contradictory, more contradictory, most contradictory.
fact: «Contradictory evidence» means clues that point in opposite directions.
fact: In science, contradictory results mean the experiment must be checked again.
fact: «Contradictory advice» means one person says do this and another says do the opposite.
exercise: «The shop is open today.» «The shop is closed today.» Are these two statements contradictory? | *Yes, they cannot both be true | They are funny statements | No, they are both true at the same time | Only on Sundays
exercise: Which word describes two statements that cannot both be true? | *Contradictory | Gentle | Cheerful
exercise: One witness says the car was green. Another says it was blue. What does the detective notice? | Both witnesses are always right | *The stories are contradictory | The stories agree perfectly | The car is invisible
test: Ben said the test was easy. Then he said it was impossible. Ben's two statements are what? | Gentle | *Contradictory | Glowing
test: Two clues in a maths puzzle say the number is both even and odd. What must happen? | Nobody needs to check | The number is zero | Both clues must be true | *One clue must be false
exam: Which pair of statements is contradictory? | *The door is open. The door is shut. | The sky is blue. The grass is green. | The bell rang at noon. The bell rang at three. | Dogs bark. Cats purr.
